# Diagnostic environment v3: where did the boot image actually go?
#
# v2 returned the real table and it has a hole in it:
#
#   1 ssd        2 persist     3 misc      4 keystore   5 frp
#   6 vm-keystore 7 vm-data    8 vm-system 9 vm-linux  10 cache
#  11 system    12 vendor     13 odm      14 userdata
#
# Fourteen entries, and they tile the disk exactly: userdata ends at LBA
# 15378418 of 15378432, leaving only the backup GPT. There is no boot, dtbo,
# vbmeta, recovery or modem partition anywhere on LUN0 -- yet `fastboot flash
# boot` keeps working and this very code boots out of whatever it wrote. So the
# ABL is not resolving "boot" against this table the way we assumed.
#
# This image reads block 0 of every partition and dumps 16 bytes of it: the
# first eight are the boot image magic ("ANDROID!" for v0/v1/v2, "VNDRBOOT" for
# vendor_boot), the next four the kernel size. Whatever currently answers to
# "boot" will show ANDROID! and a kernel size just under 0x2bb000 -- the size of
# the U-Boot image flashed to get here, which is unmistakable. That names the
# partition, whatever the ABL calls it.
#
# The three 4 MiB LUNs are checked the same way: they hold no GPT that we have
# seen, so if the image is not in any of the fourteen above, that is where to
# look next.
#
# Block 0 of each partition is identified by the block number scsi read prints,
# so no label lines are needed -- two lines per partition keeps 34 lines of
# output under the 70x76 console.
bootdelay=2
bootretry=-1

stdin=serial,button-kbd
stdout=serial,vidconsole
stderr=serial,vidconsole

preboot=echo; echo RMX1971 diag v3

bootcmd=echo === block 0 of each partition;scsi read 0xa0000000 6 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 8 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 2000 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 2100 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 2180 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 2200 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 2300 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 2d00 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 ad00 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 cd00 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 1cd00 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 125900 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 188900 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi read 0xa0000000 198900 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;echo === lun 1-3 block 0;scsi dev 1;scsi read 0xa0000000 0 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi dev 2;scsi read 0xa0000000 0 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi dev 3;scsi read 0xa0000000 0 1;md.b 0xa0000000 10;scsi dev 0;echo === end;sleep 30;reset
